  "lyrics": {
    "rawText": "\nMaybe the groove begins here  \n\nFlip the coin and call the frame  \nTruth and chaos look the same  \nIf the rule is written twice  \nDoes the error make it nice  \n\n(Or maybe that was the chorus)\n\nRandom numbers in the air  \nEvery answer almost fair  \n\nSpin the system, roll the dice  \nOnce is logic, twice is spice  \nPatterns bloom where none should be  \nRandom sings in harmony  \n\nMaybe this part was the bridge  \nOr maybe not  \n\nDuplicate the line again  \nPredicate becomes a friend  \nSay the theorem once or thrice  \nStill the groove will improvise  \n\nDeterministic gears align  \nBut chance keeps scribbling in the margin  \nNoise becomes the hidden guide  \nOrder growing deep inside  \n\n\nSpin the system, roll the dice  \nOnce is logic, twice is spice  \nRandom dancing through the code  \nEvery path a shifting road  \n\nSpin the system, roll again  \nProof dissolves but truth remains  \n\nRefresh the noise"
  },
